    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n88113" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρόξ</span></b> , gen. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">προκός, ἡ,</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>roe deer, Cervus capreolus,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἶγας ἐπ᾽ ἀγροτέρας ἠδὲ πρόκας ἠδὲ
					λαγωούς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					17.295
				</span></i>
			; coupled with <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔλαφος</span> by
				<i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>HA</u>
				506a22
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				515b34
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>PA</u>
				676b27
			</span></i>, Dionys.<i><span class="en">
				Ath.
			</span></i> and <i><span class="en">
				Philet.
			</span></i> ap. Sch.<i><span class="en">
				A.R.
				2.279
			</span></i>; but expld. as <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ τέκνον τῆς
				δορκάδος</span> by Sch.<i><span class="en">
				Nic.
				<u>Th.</u>
				578
			</span></i>, cf. Sch. <i><span class="en">
				Od.
			</span></i> l. c.:—also <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">προκάς</span></b>  (q. v.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> metaph., <i>coward,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Archil.
				188
			</span></i>.</div>
